# TradingAgents Agent Coordination

## Product Work

Use a separate worktree from current `origin/main`:

```bash
git fetch origin --prune
git worktree add ../TradingAgents-TA-<N>-<slug> -b feature/TA-<N>-<slug> origin/main
```

Docs/rules-only work may occur in the root checkout only when explicitly scoped.

## Ownership

- Read `docs/ops/in-progress.md` before editing when concurrent agents or
  worktrees are active, and record the owned scope once execution begins.
- Inspect existing worktrees and dirty files before editing.
- Do not overwrite another task's branch, worktree, files, or runtime artifacts.
- If scopes overlap, stop and resolve ownership before continuing.
- Preserve user changes; do not reset or clean them away.

## Upstream

- `origin` is the user's fork; `upstream` is the external project.
- Sync upstream on `chore/sync-upstream-YYYYMMDD` only.
- Do not combine upstream sync with product features or fixes.
- Record upstream and resulting SHAs, conflicts, resolutions, and full regression
  evidence.

## Before PR

- Fetch and compare with current `origin/main`.
- Rebase/merge only according to branch ownership and user direction.
- Run scope-appropriate gates and `git diff --check`.
- Use `--force-with-lease` only on an owned rebased feature branch; never on
  `main` or a shared branch.
